000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. BLKCHAR.
000300* BLOCK CONTAINS n CHARACTERS states the physical record size
000400* outright -- general rule 3 on IV-11 -- where RECORDS states how
000500* many logical records a block holds. 240 characters of 80-byte
000600* records is three to a block, so seven records make two full
000700* blocks and a short one. If the DCB carried the wrong BLKSIZE the
000800* file would not read back.
000900 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
001000 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
001100 FILE-CONTROL.
001200     SELECT BLK-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-BLKFILE.
001300 DATA DIVISION.
001400 FILE SECTION.
001500 FD  BLK-FILE
001600     BLOCK CONTAINS 240 CHARACTERS
001700     LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED.
001800 01  BLK-REC      PIC X(80).
001900 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
002000 01  I            PIC 9      VALUE 0.
002100 01  N            PIC 9      VALUE 0.
002200 01  EOF-FLAG     PIC X      VALUE 'N'.
002300 01  LINE-OUT.
002400     02  FILLER   PIC X(7)   VALUE 'RECORD '.
002500     02  L-NUM    PIC 9.
002600     02  FILLER   PIC X(72)  VALUE SPACES.
002700 01  SEEN         PIC X(8).
002800 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
002900     OPEN OUTPUT BLK-FILE.
003000     PERFORM WRITE-ONE 7 TIMES.
003100     CLOSE BLK-FILE.
003200     OPEN INPUT BLK-FILE.
003300     PERFORM READ-ONE UNTIL EOF-FLAG = 'Y'.
003400     CLOSE BLK-FILE.
003500     DISPLAY 'READ  ' N.
003600     STOP RUN.
003700 WRITE-ONE.
003800     ADD 1 TO I.
003900     MOVE I TO L-NUM.
004000     WRITE BLK-REC FROM LINE-OUT.
004100 READ-ONE.
004200     READ BLK-FILE AT END MOVE 'Y' TO EOF-FLAG.
004300     IF EOF-FLAG NOT = 'Y'
004400         ADD 1 TO N
004500         MOVE BLK-REC TO SEEN
004600         DISPLAY 'GOT ' SEEN.
